# Phase 15 design / Phase 15b run — see docs/v3/15-senato-exploration.md
# (design) and docs/v3/15b-senato-link-probe.md (actual run + results).
#
# Purpose: discover what predicates the dati.senato.it osr: ontology
# actually exposes on a ?senatore/?mandato resource beyond the ones
# tools/queries/senato_senatori.rq already asks for — specifically,
# whether anything resembling an elected-collegio reference exists at all.
#
# Why this is needed before writing a real collegio-join query: v2 Phase 8
# hit the exact same problem on the Camera side — the obvious-looking
# `?collegio` variable in the original query turned out to be the wrong
# granularity, and the correct field (dcterms:spatial) was only found by
# running a live predicate-enumeration query against the graph, not by
# guessing from the ontology's naming conventions. See
# docs/v2/03-linkage-report.md and CLAUDE.md's "Audit/verify before
# implementing" methodology note.
#
# Deliberately NOT aggregated (no GROUP BY/SAMPLE/COUNT) and deliberately
# NOT selecting ?value alongside ?predicate: an aggregated form got
# HTTP 400/403 from this endpoint, and a raw (?predicate, ?value) form hit
# the endpoint's apparent ~10,000-row cap almost entirely on
# osr:interviene (floor-speech records — thousands per senator), crowding
# out the low-cardinality predicates before most senators were even
# reached. SELECT DISTINCT ?predicate alone can never be truncated below
# the true distinct-predicate count (there are only ~20, nowhere near
# 10,000), so it safely enumerates the complete predicate set; per-predicate
# SAMPLE values are then fetched by a small number of separate, predicate-
# scoped follow-up queries (see docs/v3/15b-senato-link-probe.md), each
# small enough to stay well under the row cap.
#
# Run only under an explicit, deliberate refetch-protocol approval — see
# docs/v3/15-senato-exploration.md §7b for why this must never be guessed
# from the ontology's naming conventions or run automatically.

PREFIX osr:  <http://dati.senato.it/osr/>
PREFIX foaf: <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/>

SELECT DISTINCT ?predicate
WHERE {
  ?senatore a osr:Senatore ;
            osr:mandato ?mandato .
  ?mandato osr:legislatura ?legislatura .
  FILTER(?legislatura = 19)
  { ?senatore ?predicate ?value }
  UNION
  { ?mandato ?predicate ?value }
}
